14:24:07 # reported from the bench: second rev 1 board, in the second drive, came up on the first try, built with what board 1 taught. No USB console capture, no counters, checks done before power not listed. Reported, not measured here.
14:27:00 # reported from the bench: board 2 confirmed as a rev 1 board in the second dead drive. On board 2 the electrolytics (C11, C12, C13) are laid flat and J2 is the old connector reused instead of a box header, so the mechanism and host cables cannot be swapped; done because board 1 was a struggle to fit. Photos: docs/photos/pcb_rev1/.
14:28:17 # reported from the bench: board 1 fit trouble was clearance all round: cable to the Apple, shielding parts, slide fit into the carriage. No dimensions taken.
14:30:24 # decided at the bench: rev 1.1 stays open. Next build is a third rev 1.0 board, when another dead UniDisk turns up, built to the board 1/2 objectives (no J2/J3 swap, fit and clearance).
